      "message": "Yes, I\u0027m aware of the controversy of making \u0027reproducible\u0027 builds...Generally I believe it\u0027s a good idea, but as is, many targets are actually not reproducible anyway so the point is moot.\n\nI put a `date` to advise the human running the program when it was built; I found myself that I would be running an older version and it didn\u0027t pick up either my test changes, or the production code changes.\n\nA per-build SHA would also make this not reproducible, no ?\n\nAnyway, I picked `date` because of it\u0027s ordering property, versus a SHA which is unordered.  My use case is \u0027unexpected results ? Oh I built this yesterday and need to rebuild\u0027 versus \u0027What is this SHA and how do I interpret it ?\u0027",
